# Reader dev-fixture paths — see src/features/reader/devContentSeed.ts's own header comments for
# the full reasoning. Copy this file to `.env`, fill in real paths, then restart Metro WITH --clear:
#
#   npx expo start --dev-client --clear
#
# --clear is required, not optional: EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the bundle at transform
# time, so a stale Metro cache keeps serving an OLD value even after you edit this file and restart.
#
# ONLY "Big EPUB" / "Big PDF" (App.tsx's dev picker) are path-configurable this way. The plain
# "EPUB" / "PDF" tabs load bundled placeholder assets via a static require() — Metro resolves that
# at bundle time, so it cannot point at an arbitrary local path; hardcoding one there is a real,
# previously-hit bug (a hard Metro bundling failure for anyone without that exact file on disk).
#
# Point these at files under samples/fixtures/ (gitignored) — never at anything git already tracks.
# Real book content must never be committed, encrypted or not (see T4_Readme.md).
#
# PLATFORM-SPECIFIC PATH FORMAT — verified empirically on-device, both platforms, 2026-08-20.
#
# iOS SIMULATOR shares the host Mac's filesystem directly, and expo-file-system's `File` there
# accepts a bare POSIX path — no scheme needed. `$PWD/samples/fixtures/<book>` (see
# READER_MEASUREMENTS.md) is the proven recipe:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_READER_FIXTURE_EPUB=/Users/you/.../samples/fixtures/book.epub
#
# ANDROID EMULATOR is a separate VM with its own filesystem — a Mac path here throws
# "URI is not absolute" the moment devContentSeed.ts's `new File(fixturePath)` tries to construct
# it, because expo-file-system's Android side needs a real `file://`-scheme URI, not a bare path.
# TWO steps, not one:
#   1. `adb push` the file onto the emulator — NOT /sdcard/Download/: files landing there are
#      owned by `media_rw` with no "other" read bit, so the app's own (different) UID gets a
#      silent "no file is there" as if it were never pushed at all. /data/local/tmp/ is
#      world-readable (rw-rw-rw-) and works:
#        adb push samples/fixtures/book.epub /data/local/tmp/book.epub
#   2. Point this at that path WITH the file:// scheme:
#        EXPO_PUBLIC_READER_FIXTURE_EPUB=file:///data/local/tmp/book.epub
# Switching which platform you're testing means swapping this value AND restarting with --clear —
# both the push destination and the URI scheme differ, not just the leading slash.

# Absolute path to a real EPUB for the "Big EPUB" tab — see the platform note above for the exact
# format each platform needs.
EXPO_PUBLIC_READER_FIXTURE_EPUB=

# Absolute path to a real PDF for the "Big PDF" tab (same iOS/Android path-format split).
EXPO_PUBLIC_READER_FIXTURE_PDF=

# Optional: which tab is selected on a fresh launch (before you've tapped a tab yourself).
# EPUB unless this is set to exactly PDF — anything else (a typo, lowercase, etc.) falls back to
# EPUB rather than seeding a book with a format nothing can open.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_READER_FORMAT=PDF
